{#
  Plain light DOM on purpose. This screen used to be written as children of
  <sz-dashboard>, whose shadow template has no <slot>, so every one of these
  elements was discarded as soon as the component upgraded and the page showed
  nothing but the dashboard's own keyboard-hint line. sz-dashboard is the home
  hero — it takes its wordmark, taglines and links from attributes, not from
  children — so giving it a slot would have been the wrong repair. page.njk was
  the other candidate, but it wraps content in <sz-markdown> with the
  line-number gutter and the code/reading view toggle, and a centred error
  screen is not a numbered document. So: no component, a real <h1>, and the
  layout lives in base.css as .sz-404.

  The ASCII slab is decoration; the heading beside it is the text equivalent —
  the same pattern sz-dashboard uses for its wordmark.
#}
